========================================================================================
             FAMILYROOTS SANCTUARY — UNIFIED DASHBOARD ROUTING ARCHITECTURE
                                TECHNICAL EXPLANATION & AUDIT
========================================================================================

DOCUMENT TITLE: Unified Dashboard Routing & Tab Navigation Architecture
TARGET APPLICATIONS: FamilyRoots Frontend & Backend
AUTHOR: Antigravity AI Engineering Team
DATE: September 21, 2026
STATUS: Approved & Deployed

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY & ISSUE STATEMENT
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
During user testing on the Member/User Dashboard (`/user-dashboard`), users reported the following behaviors:
1. When navigating between sidebar tabs (e.g. clicking "My Profile" or "Settings"), the application unexpectedly redirected back to `/user-dashboard` (or `/`).
2. The URL briefly shifted to `/user-dashboard/profile` or `/owner-dashboard?tab=settings` and then bounced back to `/user-dashboard`.
3. In other sections, the route formatted as `?tab=tree` or `?tab=memories`, causing confusion over why some tabs used query parameters (`?tab=...`) while others used path routes (`/profile`), and why the layout was reloading.

The user requested:
- A full explanation of why this redirect occurred ("whsy").
- An explanation of how `owner-dashboard` handles routing.
- Implementation of the exact same unified `?tab=...` pattern across ALL dashboards (`user-dashboard`, `owner-dashboard`, and `admin-dashboard`).

This document details the root cause analysis, the owner dashboard reference architecture, the unified implementation across all dashboards, and validation.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS: THE REDIRECT LOOP
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The redirect bug was caused by a combination of three factors:

2.1. Re-exporting Owner Pages in Member Dashboard:
In `src/app/user-dashboard/profile/page.tsx` and `src/app/user-dashboard/settings/page.tsx`, the code was:
    export { default } from "@/app/owner-dashboard/profile/page";
    export { default } from "@/app/owner-dashboard/settings/page";

In `src/app/owner-dashboard/settings/page.tsx`:
    useEffect(() => {
        router.replace("/owner-dashboard?tab=settings");
    }, [router]);

2.2. Role-Based Route Protection (`SanctuaryDashboardWrapper` & `canAccessRoute`):
When a logged-in user with role `MEMBER` or `USER` clicked "My Profile", the browser loaded `/user-dashboard/profile`, which immediately executed the `useEffect` above:
    router.replace("/owner-dashboard?tab=settings");

Next.js transitioned the route to `/owner-dashboard?tab=settings`.
On `/owner-dashboard`, `SanctuaryDashboardWrapper` mounted and evaluated:
    canAccessRoute(pathname, user.role); // canAccessRoute("/owner-dashboard", "MEMBER")

In `src/lib/utils/roleUtils.ts`:
    if (pathname.startsWith("/owner-dashboard")) {
        return (
            normalizedRole === "OWNER" ||
            normalizedRole === "ADMIN" ||
            normalizedRole === "SUPER_ADMIN"
        );
    }
Because `normalizedRole` was `MEMBER`, this returned `false`!

2.3. The Bounce Back:
Upon failing the access check, `SanctuaryDashboardWrapper` executed:
    const targetRoute = getDashboardRouteByRole(user.role); // returns "/user-dashboard"
    router.replace(targetRoute);

Result: The member was immediately bounced back to `/user-dashboard`, creating the illusion of a broken link or an inability to navigate!

2.4. Layout Unmounting:
In addition, `user-dashboard/page.tsx` was not wrapping the entire page at the root level inside `<SanctuaryDashboardWrapper>`. Instead, subpages like `/user-dashboard/messages` each rendered their own `<SanctuaryDashboardWrapper>`. This caused the entire sidebar, navbar, and state to unmount and remount on every click.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. THE OWNER DASHBOARD REFERENCE ARCHITECTURE
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Owner Dashboard (`/owner-dashboard`) was designed around a clean, single-page container pattern:

3.1. Single Persistent Container:
`src/app/owner-dashboard/page.tsx` mounts `<SanctuaryDashboardWrapper>` once at the root level:
    export default function DashboardPage() {
        return (
            <SanctuaryDashboardWrapper>
                <Suspense fallback={<TabLoadingSkeleton />}>
                    <OwnerDashboardContent />
                </Suspense>
            </SanctuaryDashboardWrapper>
        );
    }

3.2. Tab Resolution with Normalization:
Inside `OwnerDashboardContent`:
    const searchParams = useSearchParams();
    const rawTab = searchParams?.get("tab");
    const tab = normalizeDashboardTab(rawTab);

    switch (tab) {
        case "users": return <UsersTab />;
        case "family": return <FamilyTab />;
        case "tree": return <TreeTab />;
        case "members": return <MembersTab />;
        case "relationships": return <RelationshipsTab />;
        case "messages": return <MessagesTab role="OWNER" />;
        case "memories": return <MemoriesTab />;
        case "events": return <EventsTab />;
        case "documents": return <DocumentsTab />;
        case "invitations": return <InvitationsTab />;
        case "settings": return <SettingsTab />;
        case "dashboard":
        default: return <OverviewTab />;
    }

3.3. Subfolder Deep-Linking Forwarders:
To guarantee that direct URLs (e.g. bookmarks or manual entry) work without 404s, every subfolder in `/owner-dashboard/<section>/page.tsx` forwards to the canonical tab format:
    export default function FamilyPage() {
        const router = useRouter();
        useEffect(() => {
            router.replace("/owner-dashboard?tab=family");
        }, [router]);
        return (
            <SanctuaryDashboardWrapper>
                <FamilyTab />
            </SanctuaryDashboardWrapper>
        );
    }

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. UNIFIED IMPLEMENTATION ACROSS ALL DASHBOARDS
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
We have applied this exact architecture across all dashboards:

4.1. User/Member Dashboard (`/user-dashboard`):
- `src/app/user-dashboard/page.tsx`:
  Wrapped at the root level in `<SanctuaryDashboardWrapper>` with `<Suspense>`.
  `UserDashboardContent` inspects `searchParams.get("tab")` via `normalizeDashboardTab`:
    - `tree` -> `<TreeTab role="MEMBER" currentUserId={user.id} />`
    - `members` -> `<MembersTab role="MEMBER" currentUserId={user.id} />`
    - `messages` -> `<MessagesTab role="MEMBER" currentUserId={user.id} />`
    - `memories` -> `<MemoriesTab role="MEMBER" />`
    - `events` -> `<EventsTab />`
    - `family` -> `<FamilyTab />`
    - `documents` -> `<DocumentsTab />`
    - `profile` / `settings` -> `<SettingsTab />`
    - `dashboard` / default -> `<UserOverviewTab />`

- Forwarder subpages in `/user-dashboard`:
  - `profile/page.tsx` -> forwards to `/user-dashboard?tab=profile`
  - `settings/page.tsx` -> forwards to `/user-dashboard?tab=settings`
  - `messages/page.tsx` -> forwards to `/user-dashboard?tab=messages`
  - `tree/page.tsx` -> forwards to `/user-dashboard?tab=tree`
  - `members/page.tsx` -> forwards to `/user-dashboard?tab=members`
  - `memories/page.tsx` -> forwards to `/user-dashboard?tab=memories`
  - `events/page.tsx` -> forwards to `/user-dashboard?tab=events`
  - `family/page.tsx` -> forwards to `/user-dashboard?tab=family`
  - `documents/page.tsx` -> forwards to `/user-dashboard?tab=documents`

- Sidebar navigation links in `SanctuaryDashboardWrapper.tsx`:
  All member sidebar links now cleanly link to:
    - `/user-dashboard?tab=dashboard`
    - `/user-dashboard?tab=tree`
    - `/user-dashboard?tab=members`
    - `/user-dashboard?tab=messages`
    - `/user-dashboard?tab=memories`
    - `/user-dashboard?tab=events`
    - `/user-dashboard?tab=profile`
    - `/user-dashboard?tab=settings`

4.2. Admin Dashboard (`/admin-dashboard`):
- `src/app/admin-dashboard/layout.tsx`:
  Added `AdminSidebarNav` with `<Suspense>` and updated navigation items to support both `?tab=...` and direct path routes (`/admin-dashboard/users`, etc.).
- `src/app/admin-dashboard/page.tsx`:
  Added `AdminDashboardContent` with `useSearchParams()` and `normalizeDashboardTab`:
    - `users` -> `<AdminUsersPage />`
    - `members` -> `<AdminMembersPage />`
    - `messages` -> `<AdminMessagesPage />`
    - `activity` -> `<AdminActivityPage />`
    - `analytics` -> `<AdminAnalyticsPage />`
    - `settings` -> `<AdminSettingsPage />`
    - `dashboard` / default -> `<AdminOverview />`

4.3. Owner Dashboard (`/owner-dashboard`):
- Continues to serve as the reference standard with unified `?tab=...` tabs and deep-linking forwarders.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. ARCHITECTURAL BENEFITS
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Zero Screen Flickering:
   Because the outer wrapper and sidebar remain mounted, switching tabs only swaps the inner React tree. No sidebar reload, no flicker, and instant rendering.
2. Complete Role Safety:
   No member page ever forwards or points to `/owner-dashboard`. Role-based access controls remain strictly enforced without false redirects.
3. Browser History & Bookmarking:
   Users can bookmark or share any URL (e.g. `/user-dashboard?tab=tree` or `/user-dashboard/tree`), and it will accurately load the intended tab.
4. Consistency Across Roles:
   Owners, Members, and Admins experience the exact same high-speed, cohesive navigation pattern.

